      "content": "I'm not a doctor, but I can provide general guidance. Acetaminophen (Tylenol) is generally safe when taken as directed, but overdosing can cause severe liver damage, especially for people with pre-existing liver conditions like hepatitis C. The maximum daily dose of acetaminophen for adults is 4000mg, but it's essential to check the label on your specific Tylenol product, as this can vary. Instead of focusing on the maximum dose, I recommend consulting your doctor or pharmacist for personalized advice, as they can provide guidance tailored to your specific medical needs.",
